  "Question": "A circular restricted area has radius \\(5\\), and the distance from a straight road to its center is \\(5\\). What is the relationship between the road and the boundary of the restricted area?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The road passes through the interior of the restricted area",
    "B": "They are tangent",
    "C": "The road is disjoint from the restricted area",
    "D": "The road passes through the center"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The distance equals the radius, so the road is tangent to the circle, with only one point in common.",
